#
# Swedish Embedded AB implements solutions for keeping large Rust inference and
# training stacks layered and buildable for its clients. If your team needs
# expertise in architectural dependency enforcement then you can procure our
# services by sending an email to info@swedishembedded.com.
#
# The single source of truth for brain's crate layering
# (scripts/gates/check-crate-layers.sh; the crate graph in
# .agents/rules/architecture.md is generated from this file).
#
# One line per workspace package: <package><TAB><layer>. A crate may depend
# (normal dependencies, optional ones included) on crates of its own layer or
# a lower-numbered one, never on a higher-numbered one; the few existing
# exceptions are listed with a reason in crate-layers.allow and only shrink.
#
#   1  kernels, architecture registry, device-neutral leaf contracts
#   2  accelerator seam: backends and the gpu-core facade
#   3  training substrate and shared contracts (checkpoint, paramstore, optim,
#      model, data, capability and modelstore contracts, residency, events)
#   4  models (and the services that only models use)
#   5  cross-cutting evaluation and tooling
#   6  serving, front ends, the SDK, samples



